From 6ca2b7daa3e8ab3e857004569fbc351ea8eb7446 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 23:18:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep request cleanup alive through repeated cancellation

A second Task.cancel() during handler abort or response handoff propagates
through gather() and interrupts the cleanup that the route owns. Wait for
both children without forwarding further cancellation, retrieve their
outcomes, then propagate the pending cancellation to the route caller.

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354, following local
HTTP lifetime commit 385a31417f9d484dd130ccedd868bc7c88615734.
Quality: no model arithmetic, scheduler, context, sampling or response-byte
change. Cleanup remains cooperative and may wait for an unresponsive child.
Tests: 18 lifetime cases and 12 native HTTP boundary cases pass in the
pinned candidate-38 runtime. Repeated-cancellation cases fail the prior fix.
Both wait-based and shielded-gather alternatives pass; wait avoids the
extra shield future. CPU probes repeat across fresh containers; no GPU
throughput or serving qualification claim.
Upstream status: local qualification in christopherowen/vllm#1; overlaps
canonical vllm-project/vllm#55790 and #49526, with additional edge coverage.
